A||||6||Thomas||Engine swap over the Top||||5||
Z||000000||Thomas||11-29-1999||06:19 AM||||In the next, its time to change my clutch again.(broken fingers)<BR>At my last swaps, I use the way underside.<BR>No Problem.<BR>But now, in my new garage, I have a crane under the Roof and a hole in the floor(for working under the car).<BR>So I will try to get the Engine to the top of the trunk.<BR>Has anybody done this work and can tell me how difficult it is?<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Sage||11-29-1999||06:36 AM||||I have seen this method used, but not often.  I visited a man once who has 18 fieros,(most of them parts cars, thats why I was there!) but I noticed one that had the engine out, but the cradle and tranny still in the car.  I asked him how he got that engine out without taking the whole cradle out.  He said, "Through the top, but it wasn't pretty!"  I have a mechanic friend who says he could take it out through the top, and you can, but the clearance is so minimal, I don't htink I would want to try it.  If you have a crane and a pit, can' you take it out the bottom?||||reg||5
Z||000002||chris6878||11-29-1999||08:51 PM||||One of my friends had his 84 coupe 4 cyl.. rebuild and the mechanic took it out the top.. so it is indeed a possibility...   i am getting ready to attemp the same..  putting a 87 4cyl in a 84 coupe...||||reg||3
Z||000003||chris6878||11-29-1999||09:13 PM||||Check out this link.... <BR> <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/shaun41178/Page3.html#Removing" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178/Page3.html#Removing</A>  Engine From the Top<P>||||reg||2
Z||000004||2FAST4U||11-29-1999||10:29 PM||||I have worked on Fiero's for many years and pulling the engine out of the top is no harder than on any other car. The only problem I ever have is when pulling the engine away from the transaxle enough to clear the input shaft sometimes the motor hits the pasenger side inner fender but it is plastic and can be forced back enough.<P>Good luck..||||reg||1
Z||000005||Thomas||11-30-1999||05:25 AM||||Thanks for the answers.<BR>Chris6878:<BR>This is a very good Info. Extra Thanks.<P>I try it and I shoot photos too.<BR>I post they here after I finish the job.||||reg||14
Z||000006||chris6878||11-30-1999||05:28 PM||||No problem...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">    Just keep us posted.. i am getting ready to do the same with my 84 coupe...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
